+# Stride Privacy Policy — Adaptation Template
+
+> This is a product-specific drafting aid, not legal advice. Replace bracketed fields, confirm actual production behavior, and obtain appropriate review before publishing.
+
+**Effective date:** [DATE]  
+**Developer:** [LEGAL NAME AND CONTACT]
+
+## Data Stride handles
+
+Stride processes daily step totals, estimated activity metrics, app preferences, and—only when a user starts a walk—location points needed to calculate and display that route. An active walk is written locally first. Stride does not contain advertising or third-party analytics SDKs.
+
+## Local-only use
+
+An account is optional. Without one, fitness and route information stays in the app'\''s local storage. Removing the app generally removes that local information. Device backups may behave according to the user'\''s operating-system settings.
+
+## Optional cloud sync
+
+If a user creates an account, Stride sends account identifiers, completed walk summaries and routes, daily summaries, goals, and preferences to the configured Supabase project over encrypted transport. It does not upload each live GPS sample as it is collected. Describe Supabase as a processor and add its applicable location and terms here: [DETAILS].
+
+## Permissions
+
+Motion permission supplies step totals where supported. Foreground location is used during a walk. If the user explicitly enables background recording and grants background location, location collection may continue while an active walk is in progress with the screen locked or another app open. It stops when the walk is paused, finished, or discarded.
+
+## Retention and deletion
+
+State the actual retention period: [PERIOD]. Users can delete their cloud account and synced records from Settings. They can remove local records by uninstalling the app [OR DOCUMENT FUTURE IN-APP LOCAL DELETE CONTROL]. Legal or security exceptions, if any: [DETAILS].
+
+## Sharing, security, children, rights, and changes
+
+Document subprocessors, lawful disclosures, security practices without guarantees, the intended age audience, jurisdiction-specific privacy rights and request process, international transfers, policy-change notice, and a monitored privacy contact: [COMPLETE BEFORE RELEASE].
